How can I calculate the conditional probability of rolling an even number on a six-sided die that is biased, with different probabilities for each number, using Java programming language? Also, can you provide me with the code to calculate the expected value and variance of the biased die roll?
Here's the code to calculate the expected value and variance of the biased die roll:
```java
double[] probabilities = {0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.05, 0.05, 0.3}; //replace with actual probabilities
double expectedValue = 0.0;
double variance = 0.0;
for(int i = 0; i < probabilities.length; i++) {
    expectedValue += (i+1) * probabilities[i]; //i+1 because we start counting from 1, not 0
}
for(int i = 0; i < probabilities.length; i++) {
    variance += probabilities[i] * Math.pow((i+1 - expectedValue), 2); //i+1 because we start counting from 1, not 0
}
System.out.println("Expected value: " + expectedValue);
System.out.println("Variance: " + variance);
```
To calculate the conditional probability of rolling an even number, you can first calculate the probability of rolling any even number by adding up the probabilities of rolling 2, 4, and 6 (assuming those are the even numbers on your die). Then, you can calculate the probability of rolling an even number given that the die is biased by dividing the probability of rolling any even number by the sum of all probabilities. Here's the code to calculate the conditional probability:
```java
double[] probabilities = {0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.05, 0.05, 0.3}; //replace with actual probabilities
double evenProb = probabilities[1] + probabilities[3] + probabilities[5];
double totalProb = 0.0;
for(int i = 0; i < probabilities.length; i++) {
    totalProb += probabilities[i];
}
double condProb = evenProb / totalProb;
System.out.println("Conditional probability of rolling an even number: " + condProb);
```

