Identifying and categorizing emotions in customer reviews can be a challenging task, but it is possible to create a Java program that can accurately categorize emotions. Here is a sample Java code that utilizes a machine learning algorithm to analyze customer reviews and categorize emotions:
```
import java.util.*;
import java.io.*;
public class EmotionAnalyzer {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Load the dataset of customer reviews
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(new File("customer_reviews.txt"));
        // Create a map to store the emotion categories and their scores
        Map<String, Double> emotions = new HashMap<String, Double>();
        emotions.put("happy", 0.0);
        emotions.put("satisfied", 0.0);
        emotions.put("disappointed", 0.0);
        emotions.put("frustrated", 0.0);
        emotions.put("angry", 0.0);
        emotions.put("neutral", 0.0);
        // Load the machine learning model
        Classifier classifier = new NaiveBayes();
        // Train the model with the labeled dataset
        Instances dataset = new Instances(new BufferedReader(new FileReader("labeled_dataset.arff")));
        dataset.setClassIndex(dataset.numAttributes() - 1);
        classifier.buildClassifier(dataset);
        // Analyze each customer review and categorize the emotions
        while (scanner.hasNextLine()) {
            String review = scanner.nextLine();
            Instance instance = new DenseInstance(2);
            instance.setDataset(dataset);
            instance.setValue(0, review);
            instance.setValue(1, "unknown");
            double[] probabilities = classifier.distributionForInstance(instance);
            for (int i = 0; i < probabilities.length; i++) {
                emotions.put(dataset.classAttribute().value(i), emotions.get(dataset.classAttribute().value(i)) + probabilities[i]);
            }
        }
        // Print the emotion categories and their scores
        for (Map.Entry<String, Double> entry : emotions.entrySet()) {
            System.out.println(entry.getKey() + ": " + entry.getValue() / emotions.size());
        }
    }
}
```
This code utilizes a machine learning algorithm called Naive Bayes to analyze customer reviews and categorize emotions. The program first loads a dataset of customer reviews and creates a map to store the emotion categories and their scores. It then loads the machine learning model and trains it with a labeled dataset.
Next, the program analyzes each customer review and categorizes the emotions using the trained machine learning model. It creates an instance for each review and sets the review text as the first attribute and "unknown" as the class attribute. It then uses the `distributionForInstance` method to get the probabilities of each emotion category for the given review. Finally, it updates the emotion scores in the map based on the probabilities.
After analyzing all customer reviews, the program prints the emotion categories and their scores. The scores are normalized by dividing them by the number of customer reviews to make them comparable.
Note that this is just a sample code and may not be suitable for all scenarios. You may need to modify the code to handle variations in language and context and improve the accuracy of emotion categorization.

