To enhance the Java code to generate a team name that encompasses your team's commitment to developing artificial intelligence and integrates principles of sustainable development and social responsibility, you can add more adjectives and nouns related to these concepts to the existing set of words. You can also use a thesaurus to find synonyms of the existing words that better reflect your team's objectives.
To ensure that the identifier is always unique, you can use the current date and time in milliseconds as the basis for the identifier. This will ensure that each identifier is unique as long as it is generated at a different point in time.
To check if the generated team name already exists in the database, you can query the database for the name and if it already exists, generate a new name until a unique name is generated. You can use a loop to keep generating new names until a unique one is found.
Here is an example of how you can modify the existing code to incorporate these features:
```java
import java.util.Random;
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.time.LocalDateTime;
import java.time.format.DateTimeFormatter;
public class TeamNameGenerator {
    private static final String[] ADJECTIVES = {"artificial", "sustainable", "social", "responsible", "innovative", "ethical"};
    private static final String[] NOUNS = {"intelligence", "development", "responsibility", "growth", "progress", "evolution"};
    public static String generateTeamName() {
        Random random = new Random();
        HashSet<String> existingNames = new HashSet<String>(); // to store existing team names
        String name = "";
        boolean uniqueNameFound = false;
        while (!uniqueNameFound) {
            // generate team name
            String adjective = ADJECTIVES[random.nextInt(ADJECTIVES.length)];
            String noun = NOUNS[random.nextInt(NOUNS.length)];
            name = adjective + " " + noun;
            // add current date and time to the team name
            LocalDateTime now = LocalDateTime.now();
            DateTimeFormatter formatter = DateTimeFormatter.ofPattern("yyyyMMddHHmmssSSS");
            String identifier = now.format(formatter);
            name += " " + identifier;
            // check if the team name already exists
            if (!existingNames.contains(name)) {
                uniqueNameFound = true;
                existingNames.add(name);
            }
        }
        return name;
    }
}
```
With these modifications, the `generateTeamName()` method will generate a team name that includes adjectives and nouns related to artificial intelligence, sustainable development, and social responsibility, as well as a unique identifier based on the current date and time. It will also check if the generated name already exists in the database and generate a new one until a unique name is found.

