One approach to generate a sequence of numbers from 1 to 10 with enhanced efficiency and higher scalability in Go is to use channels and goroutines. Instead of using a loop to generate the sequence, we can create a channel that sends the numbers from 1 to 10, and then use a goroutine to receive and print the numbers.
Here's an example code snippet:
```go
package main
import (
	"fmt"
)
func main() {
	seq := make(chan int)
	go func() {
		for i := 1; i <= 10; i++ {
			seq <- i
		}
		close(seq)
	}()
	for num := range seq {
		fmt.Println(num)
	}
}
```
In this code, we create a channel `seq` of type `int`, and then use a goroutine to send the numbers from 1 to 10 to the channel using a loop. We then close the channel to signal that all numbers have been sent. Finally, we use another loop to receive and print the numbers from the channel until it is closed.
